# Migrations must run before the app boots, exactly as render.yaml and
# railway.json already do. Without this, a host that honours the Procfile starts
# new code against an un-migrated database: the API looks healthy and then every
# write fails at runtime. The checkout deploy did exactly that — the pay step
# returned a 500 with "P2022: The column `subtotal` does not exist in the
# current database".
#
# `&&` is deliberate: if the migration fails the process must not start, so the
# health check fails loudly instead of serving an API that cannot take orders.
web: npx prisma migrate deploy && npm run start
